[0.123, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnc`, the `rename`, the directory's `fsync`. |                                                         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 369 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m| A message longer than a packet | Stage 4's review (4) | Manifest's snapshot of the trading scenario \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwas 63,567 bytes of the 64 KiB `maxMessageBytes`, past it with ten resting orders, and the roadmap boo\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mked splitting and reassembly. **Done** 2026-11-24 with a test and no code: a message is an ENet packet\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, which ENet splits into datagrams and reassembles already, so the limit is a setting a game raises (`\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mLimits::maxMessageBytes`). Measured on loopback: a reliable message of 1 MiB arrives; an unreliable on\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me, its fragments sent at once into the receiver's 256 KiB socket buffer, arrived twenty times of twent\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242my at 192 and 256 KiB and never at 384 KiB or more. Past that a view wants deltas, not provisioned ([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mar\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mchitecture\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](architecture.md#networking)). | Met: the `net` suite sends a 192 KiB snapshot and a 1 MiB \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mreliable message and compares each byte for byte, thirty runs of thirty. |                            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 370 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 371 \u001b[22m Manifest's W18, W11 and W19 needed no engine edit, and later W12, W13 and W14 (2026-11-23), competitiv\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m e\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m72\u001b[12G\u001b[22mprocurem\u001b[21Gnt, regional\u001b[34Ggovernance\u001b[45Gand\u001b[49Gthe\u001b[53Gclose\u001b[59Gof\u001b[62Gits\u001b[66GStage\u001b[72G4,\u001b[75Gon\u001b[78Gthe\u001b[82Gpin\u001b[86G`14fc23a`.\u001b[97GIts\u001b[101GR01\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m73\u001b[12G\u001b[22m(2026-11-24), the save and compatibility contract, a planning task, needed none either and \u001b[104Games\u001b[109Gno\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[13G\u001b[22mshell\u001b[19Gcommand…\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ (git diff --name-only; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard) | grep -E '\\\\.(cpp|h)$' | sort -u | xargs \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mclang-format -i && \u001b[26G/scripts/format-check.sh\r\u001b[15C\u001b[2B9m 29s\u001b[23G· ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m33.3k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle) · esc to inte\u001b[54Grupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
